Falsifies `system_tests::user::nth_retype_tests::login_gives_back_everything_when_any_retype_of_a_login_fails`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64 (the hunk is portable userspace code; x86_64 skips the test, as it
skips every `login_tests` test, for want of a RedoxFS disk on its test boot).

The defect is the one milestone 757 (a test kernel fails a process on its Nth retype) found and
fixed, put back for one of its three objects: `build_child_space` returns `Err` without deleting the
address space it retyped, so every failed caretaker build leaves one stale `AddressSpace`
capability in `login`'s table.

Expected to fail: retype 10, the caretaker's first frame, reported as `failing login's retype 10 of
10 (verdict 0x2) changed what login holds`, with `slot 18: AddressSpace(..)` in the table dump.
Replayed red on aarch64 on 2026-10-04 (UTC) by the lane for milestone 757.

